From f1fefadeb23fd1d5275300678f3a37d7e6622964 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:15:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1002/1002] SableOS: Files keys for copy, move, rename, new
 folder and delete

Wire the Files keyboard model into the Files app (FilesActivity; the
picker is unchanged):

* FilesActivity.dispatchKeyEvent asks SableFilesKeys first, so an Alt
  command is not typed into type-to-focus. FocusManager reports whether
  a type-to-focus search is running.
* Commands that act on files go through
  DirectoryFragment.runKeyboardAction: it uses the selection or, when
  nothing is selected, selects the focused file so the selection bar
  shows what the command applies to, builds the selection menu with
  MenuManager.updateActionMenu, and runs the item only when that menu
  would offer it, through handleMenuItemClick. So Delete still asks
  first, Copy to and Move to still open the destination picker, and
  read-only files cannot be renamed or deleted from the keyboard.
* New folder and select all use the existing option menu paths; "/"
  opens the search bar.
* Esc with no search or selection to cancel goes up one folder like
  Back (it did nothing); SharedInputHandlerTest is updated.
* The Alt shortcuts, Del and / are listed in the keyboard shortcuts
  helper next to the Ctrl ones.

Focus stays visible through the Material 3 focus ring upstream already
draws on list and grid items.
